+------------------------------------------------------------
-- @DESC: dangling for without done is rejected (E6)
------------------------------------------------------------+
rule main:
  new sum := 0;
  for i ∈ (1..5) do
    let sum := sum + i;
  -- cycle body is never closed with `done;`
+------------------------------------------------------------
Negative case: a `for` cycle whose body is closed by EOF
instead of `done;` is an unterminated block — the parser must
reject it (E0203), so the compiler exits non-zero. Analogue of
T0607 but for cycles (spec/02-statements.md §3.4, D14).
------------------------------------------------------------+
-- @AI: No - negative syntax case (passes on non-zero exit)
